/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Insight: The gender unemployment gap from 2010 to 2019 varies by region and state. The South shows the smallest and most consistent gaps, suggesting greater gender parity. The Midwest and Northeast have larger, more uniform disparities, while the West is more mixed, with both the highest and lowest state-level gaps. This highlights how regional averages can mask internal differences. Overall, gender unemployment inequality in the U.S. varies in both size and distribution across regions and states.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
