/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Insight: The data shows that crime patterns vary by income level, but not equally across all types. Property crimes like burglary and larceny-theft are more common in low-income states and decline with higher income. In contrast, motor vehicle theft is highest in high-income states. Violent crime rates remain fairly consistent across income groups, with only slight differences. This suggests income is closely linked to some property crimes but has a weaker, more complex relationship with violent crime.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
