<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Insight: This time-series chart shows unemployment trends by race compared to the national average. Early in the decade, Black and Native American groups had the highest rates, while Asian and White rates stayed below average. After 2014, Black and Native American unemployment declined, while Asian rates rose above the national average and stayed elevated. Hispanic unemployment remained consistently above the national trend. Overall, unemployment patterns vary by race and shift over time, with some groups persistently more affected than others.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
